<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nouméa Accord</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1998">1998</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/noumea">Nouméa</a> Accord, signed on 5 May 1998 by the French state and New Caledonia's independence and loyalist movements, set out a gradual transfer of powers to the territory over twenty years. It recognised Kanak identity, created a New Caledonian citizenship and provided for up to three referendums on independence, held in 2018, 2020 and 2021, each of which rejected independence.</p></div>
